{
 "id": "suffix-verbs",
 "part": "Γ",
 "el": "Ρήματα από ονόματα",
 "title": "Making verbs from nouns and adjectives",
 "level": "B1–C1",
 "intro": [
  {
   "p": "Greek turns nouns and adjectives into verbs with a handful of endings. Knowing them helps both ways: you can recognise **κοκκινίζω** as *go red* from κόκκινος, and you can produce **ζεσταίνω** from ζεστός. Each ending also decides the conjugation, so the drill will help your verb forms too."
  }
 ],
